@startuml failure-handling
!include _style.iuml
title Image download: retries, give-up and redelivery

queue "RabbitMQ\nimages" as QI
participant "image-worker\nfetch_image" as IW
participant "Image host" as HOST
database PostgreSQL as PG
queue "images.XQ\n(dead letters)" as DLQ

QI -> IW : fetch_image(image_id)
IW -> PG : load image
alt image is no longer pending (duplicate or redelivered message)
  IW -> PG : finish feed if complete\n(an earlier delivery may have died before this)
  IW --> QI : ack
else pending
  IW -> HOST : GET url
  alt 200 with image/* content type
    IW -> PG : downloaded
    IW -> PG : finish feed if complete
  else permanent: 4xx (not 429), not an image,\ntoo large, bad URL, redirect loop
    IW -> PG : failed (error stored)
    IW -> PG : finish feed if complete
  else transient (429, 5xx, timeout, connection error,\nbody deadline, time limit) or unexpected (bug, disk full)
    alt attempts left (5 retries)
      alt transient
        IW --> QI : dramatiq.Retry, exponential backoff\n1-2, 2-4 ... 16-32 s, or the host's Retry-After\n(logged at INFO)
      else unexpected
        IW --> QI : re-raised: same backoff,\nlogged with traceback
      end
    else last attempt
      IW -> PG : failed ("gave up after retries")
      IW -> PG : finish feed if complete
      IW --> DLQ : message dead-lettered (logged at WARNING)
    end
  end
end

note over IW, PG
  Every write is idempotent: image IDs are uuid5(feed_id, url),
  status changes only WHERE status = pending, and the feed
  becomes done only when it is parsed and no image is pending.
  A worker killed at any point is safe: RabbitMQ redelivers
  the unacked message (at-least-once delivery).
end note
@enduml
